{"skill":{"slug":"wordpress","displayName":"Wordpress REST API"},"version":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1770027136694,"changelog":"Initial release of the WordPress REST API CLI skill.\n\n- Provides a simple CLI for automating WordPress post, page, taxonomy, and user management via the REST API.\n- Supports JSON-in/JSON-out workflows with minimal dependencies (only native HTTP).\n- Credentials can be supplied via environment variables for Basic, App Password, or JWT authentication.\n- Allows advanced custom requests and input via file or command line.\n- Installation and setup require Node.js 18+ and WordPress REST API/application passwords.\n- Includes operational guidance and security best practices in documentation.","changelogSource":"user","license":null,"files":[{"path":"package.json","size":273,"sha256":"5f1b81eba2145457ac03b5319ea0987fa8df300b91d117e726c320acb5823b65","contentType":"application/json"},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":2470,"sha256":"afa5c7d90de454030f15d3fbcc7cfca701d62f986242d9f2e6d8acd7222ff202","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"env_example.md","size":328,"sha256":"834dc3bf6fb8d0041ad0a605bd885cc72dcbfd275d0f145df89301990a46d48b","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"assets/wordpress-rest-api-guide.md","size":1877,"sha256":"2cb72c4c8008e4e92d560db6f031528f450dad1fe4f3d89ba54575bb883048ae","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"scripts/wp-cli.js","size":8469,"sha256":"efb1952289ffab2283094eb645647bdf7cdf2691a2d8235d98e84b0ad72c4c84","contentType":"text/javascript"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":1939,"sha256":"57e2befc5dbed866e5294e8bfc17f595ab59ede324106ef8e1d3be4aa0a92291","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789028270776,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"7076bc4f4a9b091903eb77b61b6756dbf84a8e4b37507060555a07f980160a20","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/7076bc4f4a9b091903eb77b61b6756dbf84a8e4b37507060555a07f980160a20","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: wordpress\nVersion: 1.0.0\n\nThe skill is classified as suspicious due to its ability to read arbitrary local files and send their content as JSON payloads to the configured WordPress API. Specifically, the `jsonFromArg` function in `scripts/wp-cli.js` uses `fs.readFileSync` on user-provided file paths (prefixed with '@'), which could be exploited by a compromised agent or malicious user to read sensitive files (e.g., `/etc/passwd`, SSH keys) and exfiltrate them via the WordPress API. Additionally, the `request` command allows arbitrary HTTP methods and paths relative to the WordPress API root, granting broad control over the target WordPress instance.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779160862250},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":88,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":9,"checkedAt":1789028270776},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"This WordPress automation skill is coherent, but it can send reusable credentials over non-HTTPS URLs and can modify or delete live site content without confirmation safeguards.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Environment-based WordPress credentials are expected for this purpose, but WP_BASE_URL is not validated as HTTPS before Authorization headers are attached and sent.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The package has no external npm dependencies and only exposes npm scripts that run the local Node CLI; no install-time persistence or hidden setup behavior was found.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The skill discloses posts, pages, taxonomy, user reads, and raw requests, but deletion and write operations lack confirmation, dry-run, target verification, or explicit production-safety boundaries.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"No persistence, background workers, tool hijacking, or privilege-escalation mechanisms were found, but the runtime authority depends on the configured WordPress credential's role.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The CLI's WordPress content-management purpose matches its REST API capabilities, but those capabilities include high-impact create, update, delete, and raw authenticated request operations on live WordPress data.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"concern"}],"guidance":"Install only if you are comfortable giving the skill a WordPress credential that can affect your site. Use HTTPS-only WordPress URLs, a dedicated low-privilege account, and avoid giving it Editor/Admin credentials unless needed. Treat delete and raw request commands as high-risk and require human review before running them against production.","findings":"[T09] unexpected: Accepted as a material concern: the code accepts WP_BASE_URL without enforcing HTTPS while attaching Basic or Bearer Authorization headers.\n[TM1] expected: Delete endpoints for posts and pages are purpose-aligned for a WordPress admin CLI, but the artifacts provide no confirmation or target-validation guardrails.\n[LP3] expected: Network access and WP_* environment credentials are expected, but the skill does not define enforceable host or environment-variable boundaries.\n[SQP-2] expected: Authenticated create, update, and delete operations are disclosed and purpose-aligned, but high-impact live content mutation lacks safety interlocks.\n[SDI-1] expected: The raw request command is disclosed as an advanced feature and is constrained to the configured WordPress wp/v2 base, but it still allows broad authenticated methods and paths.\n[SDI-2] expected: The advanced request primitive matches the stated custom-request purpose, yet it is under-scoped for agent use because it has no allowlist or explicit dangerous-mode gate.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789028270776}}}}}